From a77b945247af82b5f7a34fd4dc858f9f9bc620a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Mostovoy <stavultras@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:18:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 38/38] target/mips, hw/mips: MT ASE multi-core CPS (MT7621: 2
 cores x 2 VPEs)

- CPS/GCR/CPC property vp-per-core: MT ASE cores of that many VPEs, the
  CPUs of a core consecutive.  GCR: PCORES, Cx_CONFIG PVPE, CM2 Cx_OTHER
  CoreNum, Cx_ID, the reset base per core; CPC: Cx_OTHER, Cx_CMD
  (PwrUp / Reset: VPE 0 from the reset base, PwrDown), Cx_STAT_CONF
  SeqState U6 while the core runs (what Linux' smp-cps waits for on CM2)
- CPU (mt_vpes): MVPConf0 PVPE/PTC, the core's VPEs share its MVP
  registers, VPE 0 of each core is the master VPE, TCBind CurVPE/CurTC
  core-local, MTTR/MFTR address the TCs of the own core, DVPE/EVPE act
  on the own core only and EVPE wakes VPEs set up while disabled
- GIC timer-routable: the CPUs' CP0 timer interrupts are GIC inputs
  (local TIMER, Vx_TIMER_MAP, masked at reset) instead of IP7
- MT7621: -smp 1 / 2 (one core, MT7621S) / 4 (MT7621A, the default);
  the NAND BootROM stub sends the cores the bootloader powers up into the
  bootloader once DRAM is up (Breed waits for core 1's coherence)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012GbUcwR34gg9RgGTEtNN6J
